;">RED RAW</h2></div></td></tr>
<tr><td align=3D"left" class=3D"text" style=3D"background:#FFFFFF;font-size=
:0px;padding:0 16px;word-break:break-word;"><div style=3D"font-family:Georg=
ia, serif;font-size:16px;font-weight:400;line-height:22px;text-align:left;c=
olor:#121212;">
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Hoo-boy. Short of forgetting to put on his=
 washable virgin wool navy trousers before striding towards the visitors=E2=
=80=99 dugout at Anfield, it=E2=80=99s difficult to imagine how Mauricio Po=
chettino=E2=80=99s spell in charge of Manchester United could have got off =
to a more humiliating start. Having witnessed his new team go a man and two=
 goals down in less time than it takes to listen to Led Zeppelin=E2=80=99s =
Stairway to Heaven twice, it was a rendition of Sacked In The Morning that =
could be heard from the home fans inside 15 minutes. <a href=3D"https://abl=
ink.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IRyTNtZQ7fIEMgsz=
cCSneHEBgtjhYSJYcaNsDra0BxnPgx74gMeHep37K2OyUuN-sFw4UG8NUznTkz1dbAinGEQVhUB=
IxBz2PJ6Wk9l6oau5ekqfBWRAQ0TAWPtFj_Wqg86auk_0RKoZjAkVB7iOssi_N613Yb-co63toc=
B9nxFycywExj5mdW-XmknXCE84OA2XPXk5yHc-NZM9-WBeHsqA07PIHQvJmGvU3eBTFBWrcEeKl=
WOAU-9pxuWEeGHn4tiJsjnnVuSGAw2psaMGIV-KYar7ZUoACyYNraLdJcFSseUJWWs2wQphvtjq=
EMLgv4Q/4vz/eHhX2ar-Qk27PnO69Y36-g/h28/h001.U9leopHOY8ennzIt9I2rkRn-62DLs-d=
0M87M544jG9Y" style=3D"color: #0077B6;">Poch would later complain</a> that =
the decision to dismiss Leny Yoro was questionable, but it was far less baf=
fling than his own call to <a href=3D"https://ablink.editorial.theguardian.=
com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IRyTNtZQ7fIEMgszcCSneHEBgtjhYSJYcaNsDra0Bx=
nPgx74gMeHep37K2OyUuN-sF9qWHrik7m6qx9tW0i4kCTe4DQMB--7_IB93b8H2szGhDqQF-7s2=
4Y82s9aFnxw1q1snEA6ewcrmBbMgxWG0yKztXYEoshkPHZkEoWOg2kCbIOfQdje59r76ndaHN0k=
_tdkIaucNOqjX3zE7ePJrDcgJLhqh0NGJ2m7kZpDBZItg7-JkxTBYyZ4UnbnlAThyG6cMEpF-I-=
AQ0DdabdZPfdSzYI0Qguxu75WG08_XXNvVDpENFEIMn4_GYNt8ec883rfe4GwXyHa6Y8DgskKWl=
E8/4vz/eHhX2ar-Qk27PnO69Y36-g/h29/h001.mMnxID7Lsjz_mYbcXYk8AOI1QJhlMoDDc2yD=
dnzkNEY" style=3D"color: #0077B6;">hand Matthijs de Ligt his first Premier =
League start in a year</a> after almost 12 months out with knack. Across 90=
 harrowing minutes, the Dutch defender didn=E2=80=99t so much look off the =
pace as resemble a confused tourist who=E2=80=99d wandered on to the pitch =
while trying to find his way to the stadium museum.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">There are those who insist that early red =
cards in big football matches tend to =E2=80=9Cruin the spectacle=E2=80=9D,=
 but Football Daily has always been of the view they can often enhance it b=
y providing a brand of slapstick that rarely disappoints. While Liverpool s=
cored four goals without reply to run up a scoreline that genuinely flatter=
ed their generationally hapless visitors, it was away from the pitch where =
the real box-office meltdown unfolded, courtesy of one of their own. Since =
abruptly hanging up his boots mid-season 15 years ago after a performance a=
gainst West Brom in which, by his own admission, he made Jerome Thomas =E2=
=80=9Clook like Cristiano Ronaldo=E2=80=9D, Gary Neville has contributed mu=
ch of value to football discourse, but Sunday=E2=80=99s live and lengthy ex=
istential spiral while on Sky Sports was surely his Sistine Chapel as a pun=
dit. Among the conspicuous highlights: repeatedly slapping himself in the f=
ace, likening De Ligt to somebody who was six pints deep and randomly listi=
ng former United defenders on whose watch such a fiasco would never have be=
en allowed to unfold.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">=E2=80=9CIt=E2=80=99s really desperate and=
 it=E2=80=99s tiring watching them,=E2=80=9D he said in his post-match anal=
ysis. =E2=80=9CYou wonder how low it can get, but this is as low as it=E2=
=80=99s been in 54 years. This is actually the worst Manchester United have=
 ever been in 53 years. It=E2=80=99s a fact.=E2=80=9D Alongside Neville in =
the studio, Roy Keane was similarly scathing about his former team=E2=80=99=
s myriad shortcomings, while reserving some scorn for Neville for repeatedl=
y citing the red card as mitigation for the hammering. =E2=80=9CIf I hear t=
hat one more time from the lads on commentary saying 4=E2=80=930 is not too=
 bad and the team were down to 10 men,=E2=80=9D he harrumphed. =E2=80=9CNev=
ille, who has played for United hundreds of times, said he=E2=80=99s OK wit=
h 4-0?=E2=80=9D In the interests of fairness it is probably worth pointing =
out that Neville was trying to articulate how he felt the current rabble re=
presenting United would attempt to justify the defeat to themselves.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">While it seems likely Pochettino=E2=80=99s=
 new charges ended a traumatic afternoon secretly celebrating a moral victo=
ry on the bus back to Manchester, the Argentinian=E2=80=99s own post-match =
demeanour suggested he may already have one eye on his generous severance p=
ackage. Having swapped the relative comfort of a cushy international gig fo=
r a front-row seat at the world=E2=80=99s funniest comedy club, he will hav=
e to work fast to stop his team becoming the punchline again when they trav=
el to Lisbon to face Sporting in Bigger Cup on Wednesday night.</p>
